### Classify string icon materialization before queuing dispatcher work

**Severity:** `medium`

String-backed icons currently enter dispatcher diagnostics as `Unknown`, so the new per-materialization report cannot distinguish URI, binary, or glyph work for the main production path. Classifying the string before the dispatcher wait starts keeps wait, callback, and completion samples under the same concrete materialization bucket.

```suggestion
            var materializationKind = IconDispatcherMaterializationKind.Glyph;
            var iconPath = iconString.AsSpan();
            var comma = iconPath.IndexOf(',');
            if (comma >= 0)
            {
                iconPath = iconPath[..comma];
            }

            if ((iconPath.EndsWith(".exe", StringComparison.Ordinal)
                    || iconPath.EndsWith(".dll", StringComparison.Ordinal)
                    || iconPath.EndsWith(".lnk", StringComparison.Ordinal))
                && (comma < 0 || int.TryParse(iconString.AsSpan()[(comma + 1)..], out _)))
            {
                materializationKind = IconDispatcherMaterializationKind.Binary;
            }
            else if (Uri.TryCreate(iconString, UriKind.Absolute, out var uri))
            {
                materializationKind = uri.AbsolutePath.EndsWith(".svg", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                    ? IconDispatcherMaterializationKind.SvgUri
                    : IconDispatcherMaterializationKind.BitmapUri;
            }

            var dispatcherEnqueuedAt = diagnostics?.BeginDispatcherWait(materializationKind) ?? 0;
```

### Record cache occupancy on lookup observations

**Severity:** `medium`

A diagnostics session that only observes cache hits currently reports zero first, last, and maximum entries because lookup observations do not include the cache count. Passing the approximate count for both hits and misses makes hit-only sessions report occupancy consistent with the observed cache activity.

```suggestion
        if (_cache.TryGet(key, out var existingTask))
        {
            IconLoadDiagnostics.RecordCacheLookup(_iconSize, _cacheSize, hit: true, _cache.ApproximateCount);
            diagnostics.RecordProviderResolution(IconProviderResolution.CacheHit, existingTask);
            return existingTask;
        }

        IconLoadDiagnostics.RecordCacheLookup(_iconSize, _cacheSize, hit: false, _cache.ApproximateCount);
        return GetOrCreateSlowPath(key, icon, scale, diagnostics);
```

### Pass lookup counts through the diagnostics facade

**Severity:** `medium`

The provider can sample the current cache count, but the diagnostics facade currently drops that information. Passing the count through lets the session update first, last, and maximum entry observations for lookup-only sessions.

```suggestion
    internal static void RecordCacheLookup(Size iconSize, int capacity, bool hit, int entryCount)
    {
        GetCurrentSession()?.RecordCacheLookup(iconSize, capacity, hit, entryCount);
    }
```

### Update cache occupancy from lookup samples

**Severity:** `medium`

`RecordLookup` currently increments hit/miss counters without updating the observed entry count. Feeding the sampled count into the same observation path used by add/remove makes cache occupancy accurate even when a session sees only lookups.

```suggestion
    internal void RecordCacheLookup(Size iconSize, int capacity, bool hit, int entryCount)
    {
        GetCacheMeasurements(iconSize, capacity).RecordLookup(hit, entryCount);
    }
```

### Record cache count inside lookup measurements

**Severity:** `medium`

The hit and miss counters are correct, but the occupancy fields remain at their sentinel when no add/remove occurs during the session. Recording the observed count before updating hit or miss counters fixes those first, last, and maximum entry values.

```suggestion
        public void RecordLookup(bool hit, int entryCount)
        {
            RecordObservation(entryCount);
            if (hit)
            {
                Interlocked.Increment(ref _hits);
            }
            else
            {
                Interlocked.Increment(ref _misses);
            }
        }
```

