### Retain only the ten slowest dispatcher outliers

**Severity:** `high`

Each slow dispatcher phase currently enqueues a new sample forever. This keeps only the ten longest samples needed by the report and drops shorter samples once the retained set is full.

```suggestion
        Interlocked.Increment(ref _dispatcherOutlierSamples);
        var sample = new DispatcherOutlierSample(
            loadId,
            inputKind,
            materializationKind,
            phase,
            isDemanded,
            startedAt,
            elapsedTicks);

        lock (_dispatcherOutliersLock)
        {
            if (_dispatcherOutliers.Count < 10)
            {
                _dispatcherOutliers.Add(sample);
                return;
            }

            var smallestIndex = 0;
            var smallestElapsedTicks = _dispatcherOutliers[0].ElapsedTicks;
            for (var i = 1; i < _dispatcherOutliers.Count; i++)
            {
                if (_dispatcherOutliers[i].ElapsedTicks < smallestElapsedTicks)
                {
                    smallestIndex = i;
                    smallestElapsedTicks = _dispatcherOutliers[i].ElapsedTicks;
                }
            }

            if (elapsedTicks > smallestElapsedTicks)
            {
                _dispatcherOutliers[smallestIndex] = sample;
            }
        }
```

### Do not keep a hidden session after ETW disables

**Severity:** `medium`

A listener can detach after the enabled check but before the hidden session is published, leaving a session rooted even though no listener remains. Revalidating after publication lets the disabled path atomically remove and stop the candidate before returning it.

```suggestion
            var candidate = new IconLoadDiagnosticsSession(
                Interlocked.Increment(ref _nextSessionId),
                retainCompletedLoadDemandStates: false);
            etwSession = Interlocked.CompareExchange(ref _etwSession, candidate, null);
            if (etwSession is null)
            {
                etwSession = candidate;
                if (!IconLoadEventSource.Log.IsEnabled() &&
                    ReferenceEquals(Interlocked.CompareExchange(ref _etwSession, null, candidate), candidate))
                {
                    candidate.Stop();
                    return null;
                }
```

### Replace cache entries atomically

**Severity:** `high`

The replacement path mutates a cache entry obtained from a non-atomic lookup, so cleanup can remove and recycle that entry before the replacement callback and `SetValue` run. Publishing a replacement entry with `TryUpdate` makes the write conditional on the dictionary still mapping the key to the same entry, and the removal notification is emitted only after that update succeeds.

```suggestion
            var replacement = new CacheEntry();
            replacement.Initialize(key, value, existing.GetFrequency() + 1.0, tick);
            if (_map.TryUpdate(key, replacement, existing))
            {
                _removalCallback?.Invoke(
                    key,
                    existing.Value,
                    AdaptiveCacheRemovalReason.Replaced,
                    ApproximateCount,
                    _capacity);
                existing.Clear();
                _pool.Push(existing);
            }
            else
            {
                Add(key, value);
            }
```

### Support exact-entry cache removal

**Severity:** `high`

Cleanup scores the enumerated entry, but a concurrent replacement can publish a fresh entry for the same key before the key-only remove runs. Adding an exact key-entry removal path lets cleanup remove only the entry it actually scored.

```suggestion
    private bool TryRemove(TKey key, AdaptiveCacheRemovalReason reason) => TryRemove(key, expectedEntry: null, reason);

    private bool TryRemove(TKey key, CacheEntry? expectedEntry, AdaptiveCacheRemovalReason reason)
    {
        CacheEntry? evicted = expectedEntry;
        var removed = expectedEntry is null
            ? _map.TryRemove(key, out evicted)
            : ((ICollection<KeyValuePair<TKey, CacheEntry>>)_map).Remove(new KeyValuePair<TKey, CacheEntry>(key, expectedEntry));

        if (removed && evicted is not null)
        {
            Interlocked.Decrement(ref _entryCount);
            _removalCallback?.Invoke(key, evicted.Value, reason, ApproximateCount, _capacity);
            evicted.Clear();
            _pool.Push(evicted);
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }
```

### Remove only the cleanup-scored cache entry

**Severity:** `high`

Cleanup should pass the enumerated entry into the exact-removal helper. Otherwise a fresh replacement for the same key can be evicted based on stale score data from an older entry.

```suggestion
            var overCapacity = ApproximateCount > _capacity;
            if (score < 0.1 || overCapacity)
            {
                TryRemove(
                    key,
                    entry,
                    overCapacity ? AdaptiveCacheRemovalReason.Capacity : AdaptiveCacheRemovalReason.LowScore);
            }
```
